# component: dropdown-menu
# decisions: A11Y-13, BRD-1, DOC-1, DOC-2, FRM-4, INT-1, OVL-13, OVL-14
# hunks:
#   OVL-13: two hosts, because upstream has two. `DropdownMenuContent` opens its own
#     `Menu.Portal`, so it reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and attaches it to the Positioner
#     inside it; the exported pass-through `DropdownMenuPortal` wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying the same class, so the escape hatch is scoped too.
#   OVL-14: `DropdownMenuContent` forwards a `container` to its `Menu.Portal`. Upstream forwards
#     none, and a portal defaults to `document.body` — which the Fullscreen API paints the
#     fullscreen element OVER, so a fullscreen player's settings menu renders invisibly behind
#     it. `DropdownMenuSubContent` takes it for free: it IS a `DropdownMenuContent`. The prop is
#     optional and `undefined` is upstream's own default, so no existing caller moves.
#   INT-1: `cursor-default` is removed from the item, the submenu trigger, the checkbox item and
#     the radio item, so a menu row shows the hand cursor the one global rule in `base.css` gives
#     every `[role^="menuitem"]`.
#   FRM-4: `data-disabled:pointer-events-none` is dropped from the item, the checkbox item and
#     the radio item, so a disabled row stays hoverable and a Tooltip can explain why.
#   BRD-1: `DropdownMenuContent` and `DropdownMenuSubContent` each draws a real 1px `border border-border` instead of upstream's
#     `ring-1 ring-foreground/10` box-shadow outline (MK reversed BRD-1 to ours, 23-09-2026). A
#     border survives forced colours and matches `foundations/elevation`; nothing else moves.
#   A11Y-13: the destructive `DropdownMenuItem`'s focused ink `focus:text-destructive` becomes
#     `focus:text-destructive-text`. Upstream paints the fill as ink on its own `/10` tint
#     (3.99:1 in light, under the AA floor); the family's `-text` ink clears it. The resting ink
#     and the icon ink stay upstream's.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
